From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 10:47:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] CODE-LOOP-CONTROL-PLANE-1: the code loop may always change
 qnfo-fleet-control, qnfo-ops, qnfo-deploy-guard and its own code
 (qnfo-fleet-control 0.35.0, qnfo-code-orchestrator 0.19.0, pillar autonomy)

Owner directive 2026-10-19, verbatim: "The code loop SHALL ALWAYS BE ABLE TO change qnfo-fleet-control, qnfo-ops, qnfo-deploy-guard and the
loop's own code." (human_actions 115 had asked for qnfo-fleet-control alone and was closed at birth on its "The deny stays" default.)

- CM_LOOP_CANARIED (fleet-control) and PLAN_LOOP_CANARIED (orchestrator) gain qnfo-fleet-control, qnfo-ops, qnfo-deploy-guard and
  qnfo-code-orchestrator; fold-guard.test.mjs holds the copies equal and requires a CP_CANARY_WORKERS /health canary, a canary_revert.py
  CANARY_WORKERS entry and a FUNCTIONAL check for each (all four already have them); the scorer host, the scorer and the container pilot stay denied.
- cmScope, the planner scope and intake accept the four workers (with their mirror); tpOnControlPlane no longer routes their levers to sessions;
  scripts/code-task-* leaves CM_SCRIPT_DENY in both copies.
- migrations/2026-10-19-code-loop-control-plane.sql: control-plane-deny applied, failure mode + code-read detector, decision_log row.
- Tests updated to use qnfo-observability as the denied example and to pin the four as in scope; CLAUDE.md and the architecture self-model updated.

Charter pillar: autonomy.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
