based) by re-applying those edits at the merge base and bumping the VERSION as the publisher does, instead of the parked ctx.patch that was cut against the old base; its revert inverts the edits on today's main. The first rebuilt branch to pass REBASE-BRANCH-ACCEPT-1 (codeagent-3oa9p0pglnnj-r2, 17:20Z) was refused at this gate ("the verified patch does not apply to idea-hub/deployed-current.worker.js at the merge base 0ac2898"), so the no-model rebase path still produced no pull request. */ /* 0.11.1 OWNER-LOCAL-INGEST-1b (2026-10-07, pillar cost, agent_issues 2080): the gateway log ingest asks the API for paid non-Workers-AI rows after its cursor (filters cost gt 0, provider neq workers-ai, created_at gt cursor), oldest first, 20 pages a tick, so the cursor only ever advances over rows it ingested and a 7-day backfill completes over a few ticks; 0.11.0 read the newest 500 of all rows newest first (418,943 in the gateway, 69 of each 100 Workers AI), reached 7 hours back on its first tick, moved the cursor to the newest row and attributed none of the 4,991 untagged DeepSeek requests of the week (measured 2026-10-07T16:15Z, about $15). Cursor key owner_local_cursor_v2:<gateway>; the v1 key is removed; the event meta reports more and remaining. Also REBASE-BRANCH-ACCEPT-1 (pillar autonomy): cmOpenDecide and cmDecide accept a task's -r<n> rebuilt branch (cmTaskBranch), so a REBASE-REQUEUE-1 rebuild gets its pull request (codeagent-3oa9p0pglnnj-r2 was refused as "not a code-loop branch" at 15:20Z, the path's first live instance); and ISSUE-NOTE-NEWLINE-1: the merge runner's note on a source issue (and the evolve merge note) starts on its own line instead of " | " on the issue's last line, which was the code-anchor: line of 10 open ACT-BRIDGE-1 issues, so their retries ran anchor-less (migrations/2026-10-07-issue-note-newline.sql repairs the open rows). */ /* 0.11.0 OWNER-LOCAL-INGEST-1 (2026-10-07, pillar cost, agent_issues 2080): the hourly tick reads each AI Gateway's request log since a per-gateway cursor and attributes the paid cost: untagged requests (the owner's desktop clients) to ai_spend_owner_local, requests tagged by a fleet worker that keeps no ledger of its own to ai_spend_ledger under that worker; cost_attribution_gap_pct counts both (it read 98 with $21.77 of 7-day DeepSeek cost unattributed), the dashboard gets owner_local_cost_usd_30d. */ /* 0.10.0 SCOPE-SCRIPTS-1 (2026-10-07, pillar autonomy, issue 2101): the merge runner's scope gains kind "script": scripts/*.py and scripts/*.mjs that are not CI gates or guards, suites, deploy primitives or the loop's own runners (CM_SCRIPT_DENY), so a fleet script defect can be a code task instead of session work (issue 2025 sat with a session-task line for scripts/cf_ops_actions.py only because of the scope). A script merges on gate, mirror-guard and comparator (deploy-gate runs the script selftests) and is verified at merge; nothing deploys it. */ /* 0.9.1 GOAL-REVIEW-HARM-1 (2026-10-07, pillar autonomy): the goal reviewer also answers harm (true when any changed line is wrong: breaks or removes kept behaviour, adds code that can never run, miscounts, contradicts a stated rule, would throw), and harm refuses whatever the verdict. The first live review (ct_hdaim0vx7h7vvl, 08:40Z, gpt-oss-120b) answered partial while naming two errors, an unreachable else that still incremented diversity_held and owner rows not forced to ACCEPT, so the runner opened PR 765, which a session closed as superseded by PR 762. A cached review without harm decides as before. 0.9.0 0.9.0 GOAL-REVIEW-1 (2026-10-07, pillar autonomy, docs/ENSEMBLE-POLICY.md): before the merge runner opens or merges a code-loop pull request, one Workers AI model from a family other than the proposer's (CM_REVIEW_MODELS gpt-oss-120b, deepseek-v4-flash, llama-3.3-70b; ops_config code_goal_review_models) reads the goal and the head diff and answers implements, partial or no; "no" refuses the task with the defects it names, which reach the intake retry through CI-FEEDBACK-1. One call per head, cached in cloud_ops_events goal-review-<task>-<head>, metered as purpose goal-review; no AI binding or ops_config code_goal_review_enabled off skips it; three unreadable replies let the checks decide (recorded). Of the three tasks self-repair rescued on 2026-10-06/07, #2052's patch only passed [] to the removed deposit stage and #1815's wrote living-paper columns no migration creates and labelled a paper "proved" when its body said "proof"; no check could see either. Also 0.8.2 MERGE-VERIFY-ATTEMPTS-1 (2026-10-07, pillar autonomy): the merge runner's verify gate accepts a task that verified after SELF-REPAIR-1 retries (attempts below CM_TASK_MAX_ATTEMPTS 9, the orchestrator's MAX_ATTEMPTS * RETRY_ROUNDS, parity-tested) instead of attempts below 3; step done with no last_error stays the record of a passed verify, and the required checks still gate every merge. The old bound refused all three tasks self-repair rescued (ct_yop1itun7a9ulz #1815, ct_vdgdp57qdszmkb #2052, ct_i0b4q32jxbvia7 #2055), each a failure in code_task_success_rate_30d with a verified patch. 0.8.1 0.8.1 MVP-FOLD-NOTDEPLOYED-1 (2026-10-07, pillar core, agent_issues 2090-2094): a folded MVP component is judged by its fold host unless its own audit row still serves (SYNC, CRON_ONLY or http 200); 0.4.129 deferred to the host only while the old script was absent from the audit or RETIRED_PRESENT, so after cf-ops delete-worker its row read NOT_DEPLOYED (404) and calendar-api, fleet-exec, qnfo-autonomy-scorer, qnfo-paper-indexer and qnfo-paper-reviser filed CHARTER-MVP-DOWN-1 while every host was SYNC. 0.8.0 0.8.0 CI-FEEDBACK-1 (2026-10-07, pillar autonomy): when a required check fails on a code-loop pull request, the merge runner reads that job's log and records the failing suites and assertion lines (cmFailureLines, at most 10 lines) in the refusal, so the task's merge_note and its issue say what broke and the next intake retry carries it; before this the note said only "gate=failure" and every retry was blind (PR 750 broke qnfo-ipatent/mechanism.test.mjs, PR 752 changed a value quality.test.mjs:190 pins). merge_note and last_error keep 1200 characters (was 500). 0.7.1 (2026-10-06, pillar autonomy): CHARTER_VERSION 1.0.11 in parity with the charter, which adds decision rule 10 "decide, then record" (RULE-8-RETIRED-1, owner directive 2026-10-06: core prompt rule 8 is deleted); one comment no longer cites rule 8. 0.7.0 CONTROL-PLANE-SELF-MERGE-1 (2026-10-06, transformation lever T1.21, pillar autonomy; owner directive 2026-10-06: more flexibility and autonomy, decide for itself): the stale-PR lane merges a green, quiet session pull request that changes a control-plane worker (CM_DENY) when ops_config control_plane_self_merge is on, the worker has a /health canary (CP_CANARY_WORKERS) and the pull request carries worker.js with its mirror; canonical-deploy.yml canaries /health for the new VERSION and reverts the push on its own (scripts/canary_revert.py, CONTROL-PLANE-CANARY-1), which replaces CONTROL-PLANE-MANUAL-1 (decision (a), human_actions 21, migrations/2026-10-06-control-plane-self-merge.sql). Workflows under .github/ still never auto-merge; the code loop still neither plans nor merges control-plane workers. 0.6.2 CRAWL-VERIFIED-GOOGLEBOT-1 (2026-10-06, pillar reach): the crawl-health view counts only requests from Google's published Googlebot ranges (googlebot.json, fallback 66.249.64.0/19); spoofed Googlebot scans are reported, not counted; a robots.txt 404 is not a failure; sitemap failures only for CRAWL_SITEMAPS. 0.6.1 (2026-10-06, pillar cost): CHARTER_VERSION 1.0.10 in parity with the charter, which records BUDGET-SOFT-ROUTE-1 (owner directive: AI spend caps steer model choice and never stop work). 0.6.0 PROBE-TRANSPORTS-1 (2026-10-06, pillar autonomy; owner directive OWNER-NO-LOOSE-ENDS-1): remediation contracts can check public sources outside the fleet: transport external-https (GET or