branch_pushed code tasks (no advance, no merge decision, no reconciliation, no day heartbeat) and stands aside at minute 0 where the hourly tick runs; measured 2026-10-06, a pushed codeagent branch waited 40-50 min for its PR on every task (pr_opened_at always hh:00) and 5 h overnight because only the hourly tick opened them, while code-task-publish had pushed the branch within a minute. CHARTER-1.0.9: CHARTER_VERSION 1.0.9 for the charter's TRANSFORMATION-PROGRAM-1 input pointer (PR 664), charter-guard C5 parity, no behaviour change. 0.4.129 MVP-FOLD-AWARE-1 (pillar core, #1756): an MVP component recorded as folded into a host (worker_removals action folded, target host) serves when its host serves, so folding a core worker under the owner standing grant does not file CHARTER-MVP-DOWN-1; the note reads FOLDED:<host>/<host note>. 0.4.128 0.4.128 REMEDIATION-PENDING-PREFIX-1 (pillar autonomy): a probe observation that starts with 'pending' (the 'pending: <reason>' form six live contracts use) is a deferral like a bare 'pending': it neither breaks a hold, reopens a closed issue, counts toward max_attempts nor ends a pass streak; 0.4.127 0.4.127 ATTRIBUTION-COVERAGE-DTD-1 (agent_issues 1997, pillar cost): workers_ai_attribution_coverage_pct is the day-to-date ratio (attributed neurons today / GraphQL neurons since 00:00Z), capped at 100, and is left unchanged while today's GraphQL total is under 5000 neurons; the hourly delta (73.2 at 19:00Z on 2026-10-05 while day-to-date read 100) filed METRIC-FIX-RELAPSED-1 on one bursty hour. 0.4.126 CREDIBILITY-CITATION-DEDUPE-1 (agent_issues 1838, pillar reach): perfCredibility no longer counts external_mentions rows whose source is an OpenAlex/Crossref/DataCite/Semantic Scholar citation feed (qnfo-cloud-ops jobRadar files every OpenAlex citation there too) as a third-party mention; citations count once, through the selected-works growth term, and the detail reports citation_mentions_not_counted. 0.4.125 0.4.125 CHARTER-1.0.8 (owner standing decision 5, 2026-10-05, pillar autonomy): CHARTER_VERSION 1.0.8 for the owner's standing grant OWNER-STANDING-GRANT-1 (charter decision rule 9: retire low-value workers after a dependency check, delete unused databases after a verified backup, switch to cheaper models with fallback and automatic revert, no owner card); charter-guard C5 parity, no behaviour change. 0.4.124 0.4.124 DRIFT-CONFIRM-2 (agent_issues 1993, pillar core): drift_total's terms (ghost, unregistered, unversioned, repo_live) are computed by one pure function; a non-zero first read is re-read once after 20s and the smaller value is written (the 18:00:13Z read of 1 sampled the inputs while the deploy batch, the self-audit and the registry sync were writing them; PR 636 DRIFT-AUDIT-AFTER-DEPLOY-1 re-audits after each deploy, this change stops the sample from being written); a non-zero first read leaves a cloud_ops_events row (kind drift-total-detail) naming the workers behind each term. 0.4.123 REMEDIATION-HOLD-1 (agent_issues 1297, pillar autonomy): a remediation contract that passes no longer stops; it holds, read once a day, and closes only after a 7-day pass streak (RT_HOLD_D), so a closure that breaks again inside the window reopens through REMEDIATION-REOPEN-1 (the 2026-09-28 closures 1283, 1284 and 1287 passed once and broke within hours after their contracts had stopped); a relapse returns the contract to active. 0.4.122 is left to session_013sMN4pr2RGmHezM4Gm6fMk (#1838). 0.4.121 REMEDIATION-REOPEN-1 fix (agent_issues 1297): an observation of 'pending' (the deferral convention, written by this tick and by remediation-consumer) neither reopens a closed issue nor counts toward max_attempts; 0.4.119 would have reopened 1919 and 1920 on their third pending row. 0.4.120 Q08-SELF-TUNE-1 (agent_issues 1760, pillar reach): PERF_LEVERS gains q08-temperature (q08_gate_pass_rate_7d, ops_config q08_compose_temperature 0.4..0.8 step 0.1, direction -1, effect higher, eval 14 days, capped by the q08 review lock); a lever step is rounded to 4 decimals so a 0.1 step never writes 0.5500000000000000. 0.4.119 REMEDIATION-REOPEN-1 (agent_issues 1297, pillar autonomy): remediationContractsTick reads the issue status; a contract on a wontfix issue is marked superseded, and a contract whose probe fails max_attempts times after its issue was closed (or since its last pass) reopens that issue once, with the failure and the prior close_evidence in its description (59 contracts had failed hourly on closed issues with nothing acting on it; INTEGRITY-GUARDS-1: a failing probe on a closed issue is a closure that did not hold); verification rows are never deleted. 0.4.118 (2026-10-05, remediation B2): LAND-BUNDLE-GUARD-1 (issues 1976, 1979): landFix refuses to commit a deployed script that adds esbuild __name helper layers or keeps under half of main's comment lines (the 2026-10-04 qnfo-fleet-dashboard 1.21.4 landing replaced the hand-written source with a wrangler bundle) and files one LAND-BUNDLE-REFUSED-1 issue instead; REPO-LIVE-DRIFT-1 (issue 1879): drift_total adds the fleet self-audit's DRIFT and CONTENT_DRIFT rows (live version or script sha256 differs from main) and counts a missing or 26h-old audit as 1; CF-CHANGELOG-LEADS-1 (issue 1959): a launch of a proposed or not_considered catalog row writes a dated when_to_choose line (max 5 a day) and GET /cf-changelog lists cost, speed and consolidation leads; CLEF-CANDIDATE-1 re-landed (PR 586 closed unmerged): clef_candidate_calls_7d is written hourly; IMPROVEMENT-UNMEASURED-STAMP-1 (issue 1865): the improvement loop stamps last_refreshed with state UNMEASURED while its trend metrics have too little history. 0.4.117 merge lane (agent_issues 1965, 1960, 1975, 1877, 1928; pillar autonomy): STALE-PR-MERGE-FIRST-1, a session pull request quiet for 2h whose required checks are green and whose mergeable_state is clean is merged by the branch sweeper (squash, pinned to the tested head) instead of being closed unmerged at 24h (PR 586 was closed green); never a draft, a do-not-merge or WIP PR, a .github/ change, a fork or a codeagent-/evolve/ branch; kill switch ops_config stale_pr_merge_enabled. MERGE-RUNNER-REFUSAL-TAXONOMY-1: a merge-runner refusal ends the code task 'failed' and hands it to the fleet (a note on its source issue, or one CODE-MERGE-REFUSED-1 issue), not an owner card. NOCHECKS-CONFLICT-1: no checks on a conflicted PR is a stale base at once; MERGE-NOCHECKS-REOPEN-1: no checks on a clean PR after 3h closes and reopens it once with the fleet token before refusing. CODE-CLOSE-REASON-1: a PR closed outside the runner records who closed it (CYCLE-TIME-1 or someone else). MERGE-RUNNER-VERSION-FORM-1: `var VERSION="x"` without spaces or semicolon is bumpable and revertible. CRON-ONLY-VERIFY-1: a cron-only worker (worker_live_audit CRON_ONLY) is verified by its fleet_heartbeat VERSION, not reverted on http null (ct_02oohvsbf1gbji). 0.4.116 IDEA-BUILDABLE-TRUTH-1: an idea is buildable only when it carries an edit point; 0.4.115 0.4.115 CYCLE-TIME-1 (2026-10-04, issue 1961): branch sweeper graces shortened to 12h closed-PR / 24h orphan / 1 day needs_human, and a stale open pull request (head not a live code task, idle over BH_STALE_PR_H 24h) is archived, commented and closed each tick so the open-PR backlog turns over inside a day. 0.4.114 MERGE-RUNNER-UNSTICK-1 (qa 2026-10-04, agent_issues 1960 PR-LANE-ZERO-TOUCH-1): GitHub computes mergeability lazily and main moves every few minutes (ci(status) commits), so the merge runner's single read per hourly tick returned mergeable=null for a green pull request every time (PRs 564, 550, 551 sat published with all checks green while none merged); it now re-reads up to CM_MERGEABLE_READS times within a tick, and takes candidates round-robin by merge_checked_at so a stuck five no longer fills every tick. 0.4.113 BRANCH-HYGIENE-2: the branch sweeper keeps the branch of a code task the merge runner refused (needs_human) for 7 days after its last update, so the branch a person has to act on is not archived and deleted after the 48h grace; GET /branch-hygiene reports needs_human_days */ /* 0.33.18 REVIEW-NO-VERDICT-1 (issue 2909): cmReviewParse reads a verdict written outside JSON and logs a reply with none as a classed, counted warning (empty, truncated-json, unknown-verdict, prose), not an error; the review already retries. FLEET-HEARTBEAT-SELF-1 (issue 2397): every scheduled tick upserts this worker's fleet_heartbeat row. */ /* 0.33.15 TEMPO-5M-1 (2026-10-18, owner directive: heartbeat/tick tempo shall not exceed 5 minutes, no time-related schedule above 120 minutes): the fast lane (code merges, branch lane, deploy-drift runner, SLA tick, remediation contracts) moved from a 10-minute trigger to a 5-minute trigger. The 20-minute grid is now a TRUE 20-minute grid on the 5-minute tick (slotMin % 20 < 5 => :00, :20, :40); the previous Math.floor(slotMin/10)%2 was a 10-minute-period test that would have fired those steps 6x an hour on a 5-minute trigger. The internal fast-lane token string is unchanged so the slice-based tests and the CRON-DISPATCH-ELIMINATION-1 fallback keep their meaning. */ /* 0.33.14 NO-UNTRACKED-CLOSE-2 (2026-10-18, owner audit closeout): the CYCLE-TIME-1 stale-PR closer closed a pull request on age alone. Two of the 32 unmerged loop pull requests (768, 752) went that way while a successor task for the same issue was still in flight, so age was not evidence that the change was unwanted. The closer now refuses while another OPEN pull request carries the same "[issue #N]": the successor must be live before the redundant one is closed. That is the last close path in this worker that could drop work without a successor; a refusal is logged as branch_hygiene_log action 'successor-open'. */ /* 0.33.13 NO-UNTRACKED-CLOSE-1 (2026-10-18, owner audit of pull requests closed unmerged): 94 loop pull requests, 62 merged, 32 closed unmerged; one of the 32 (PR #2113, CROSS-FAMILY-1) was a real loss. REBASE-REQUEUE-1 closed it on the promise that "the rebuilt branch opens its own" pull request - the rebuilt branch never opened one, the task ended 'closed' with merged_at NULL, and main never carried the change, so the close discarded the only copy of that work. The rebase path now parks the number in ctx.superseded_pr and closes nothing; cmCloseSuperseded() (one call a tick, beside the publish dispatch) closes the parked pull request only once the task has a DIFFERENT live pull request or has merged. An unmerged pull request is never closed on a promise, and never while it is the task's only copy. Fail-safe direction: a bug here leaves a pull request open, never a change lost. */ /* 0.33.12 CARRIED-BY-TWIN-1 (2026-10-18 audit follow-up): a contract on a CLOSED issue whose title has an OPEN twin with its own live contract can never reopen (REMEDIATION-REOPEN-2 and rtReopenOnRelapse both refuse while a twin is open, agent_issues 2902), so it probed a dead issue for ever - 9 issues, 170 rows in one day, worst issue-2194 at 196 rows. It is now superseded as 'superseded:carried-by-twin' and the twin's own contract verifies the predicate. Audit context: the closed-issue failure class is dominated by closures accepted on proxies (code task merged, build deployed, TRIGGER-RECOVERY fired) while the contract that measures the actual predicate still fails - 482 of the 893 closed-issue failures on 2026-10-18; the fix for that is single closing authority (agent_issues 2953), not a cadence change. */ /* 0.33.11 DEFERRAL-NOT-A-FAILURE-1 (2026-10-18, fleet-wide verification audit): 19,320 of 135,263 remediation_verifications rows (14.3%, and 31.5% of all 61,282 pass=0 rows) were 'pending' deferrals - a probe that cannot judge yet, written as a hard failure, which is the whole origin of the "45% of verification runs fail" reading. The tick now yields verdict 'deferred', writes no verification row, and logs the reason once per class per 6 h; the reopen, pass-streak and hold rules already excluded 'pending' by SQL, so no other behaviour moves. Audit finding recorded beside it: the row-level ratio counted re-probes, not outcomes; the canonical split is view v_verification_verdict_split (pass / real-fail / deferral / detector-breach / placeholder). */ /* 0.33.10 CF-OBS-SWEEP-1 (2026-10-18): pollObservability reads ALL pages of the Cloudflare Observability issues list (the old read was page 1 only, so 25 of 125 groups were invisible), classifies each group (external vulnerability-scan noise -> ignored; a group quiet for CF_OBS_STALE_H -> resolved; a live recurring defect -> left active for FLEET-JOURNEYS-2 traffic-health), PATCHes the Cloudflare status so the active list converges to real defects, and writes one cf_obs_sweep_runs row per poll (the audit ledger for fm-cf-obs-sweep-stale). Also REMEDIATION-REOPEN-TWIN-1: rtReopenOnRelapse no longer flips a closed issue to open when an open twin with the same lower(trim(title)) already exists (the partial unique index idx_agent_issues_open_title_ci threw 241 SQLITE_CONSTRAINT_UNIQUE collisions in 2 h). */ /* 0.33.9 POOL-BOUND-1 (2026-10-18): the research deferred pool is bounded at ops_config research_deferred_max (default 60, the registered research_deferred_pool target); lowest-priority overflow is parked with a revert line and re-armed automatically when the pool falls below half the bound. */ /* 0.33.8 PROBE-ERROR-VISIBILITY-1 (2026-10-17): 529 of 973 active contracts reported probe-error and the exception was swallowed, so the failure could not be attributed; the message is now logged and written to cloud_ops_events (deduped hourly). 0.33.7 SLA-PATHS-1 delta: readers read v_remediation_evidence_all, a path-B pass closes in code, path liveness is measured. */ /* 0.33.7 SLA-PATHS-1 delta (2026-10-17, owner directive): 0.33.6 wrote path B but nothing read it - the hold/reopen readers still counted remediation_verifications alone, so fallback evidence was write-only and no issue closed. Readers now read v_remediation_evidence_all; a path-B pass closes its issue in code after the same 7-day streak with close_evidence naming the row; path liveness is measured (path_liveness + a daily B drill) and fewer than two live paths files SINGLE-PATH-1. */ /* 0.33.6 SLA-AND-PATHS-1 path B (2026-10-17, owner directive "ALL STEPS, ALL PROCESSES SHALL HAVE SLA AND MULTIPLE EXECUTION/REMEDIATION/WORKAROUND PATHS"): remediation_verifications has seven triggers and every INSERT into it has failed with "triggers nested too deep" since 15:08:58Z (issue 2794); the trigger-free sink remediation_evidence existed but no code wrote to it, so evidence was lost and autoclose/reopen never fired. All three insert catches now fall through to the sink. // 0.33.3 TICK-ERROR-VISIBILITY-1 (2026-10-17, fleet-wide audit): the two verification inserts added by PROBE-NULL-OBSERVED-1 ran bare, so any refusal became "probe-error" and the verdict was silently lost; 62 of 70 contracts in the 15:18Z pass reported probe-error and wrote no row, which also stops the reopen/autoclose triggers from ever seeing evidence. Both inserts now log their real message and still yield a verdict. */ /* 0.32.0 GH-APP-BROKER-1 (2026-10-14, pillar autonomy/security): the GitHub App qnfo-fleet installation token, minted from GH_APP_PRIVATE_KEY/GH_APP_ID/GH_APP_INSTALLATION_ID and cached until 5 minutes before expiry, is every invocation's GITHUB_TOKEN; a GitHub request it is refused (401/403/404) is replayed once with the personal token; ops_config gh_app_primary = off restores the personal token; GET /gh-app reports the path; the 10-minute tick writes github_app_token_ok and scheduler_state gh_app_broker. */ /* 0.31.2 (2026-10-14, pillar autonomy): SLA-120M-7, owner directive 2026-10-14 (no SLA exceeds 120 minutes, measured at 10-minute resolution): the merge runner's check and deploy waits (CM_CHECKS_WAIT_MIN, CM_DEPLOY_WAIT_MIN) and the evolve CI and deploy waits (EVOLVE_WAIT_MIN) are 120 minutes, not 3 h; the drift redeploy cooldown is 120 minutes, not 6 h, and its refusal names it (it named a 60-second cooldown); evaluateMetricTriggers reads the re-fire wait in minutes, at most 120 (an empty column was 24 h); the seeded metric triggers start at a 2 h cooldown, not 168; the unused 2-hour merge-idle constant is gone. */ /* 0.31.1 (2026-10-14, pillar core): JRN-CLOCK-1 the traffic-health journey measures its 6 h window from the tick's clock, so journeys.test.mjs no longer fails once the wall clock passes its fixed NOW; JRN-ASK-TIMEOUT-1 the ask-path journey hop waits JRN_ASK_TIMEOUT_MS (60 s) for an answer that streams for 15-30 s instead of the 12 s every hop had, and a stream cut by a timeout after its status arrived is reported as a timeout, not as "0 events" (agent_issues 2574). */ /* 0.31.0 (2026-10-14, pillar autonomy; owner directive ISSUE-SLA-2H-1): SCHEMA-ALTER-PROBE-1 evSchema and cfcSchema read their columns before an ALTER, as cmSchema does, because Workers telemetry recorded each caught "duplicate column" ALTER as an exception (14 every hourly tick; agent_issues 2562). IL-DEFECT-ONLY-1 IMPROVEMENT-LOOP-1 files a regression only when the metric is off target now (a decline inside the target is an early warning kept in the run state and GET /improvement), closes an open regression or relapse issue whose metric is back inside its target as an early warning, and closes one an open trigger issue carries as superseded by it (2551 and 2193, 2223 and 2284 sat open side by side); DRIFT-HEAL-GRACE-1 the drift scan redeploys a worker only after main has been ahead of it for 20 minutes, so it no longer races the canonical deploy of the same push for the deploy-guard lock (2391, 2547; qnfo-cloud-ops 2026-10-14 03:01:31). */ /* 0.30.0 SLA-TICK-10M-1 (2026-10-14, pillar autonomy; owner directive "All SLAs systemwide across the fleet shall be measured in 10-minute intervals/resolution, never hours or days. No SLA shall ever exceed 120 minutes and action shall commence immediately >120 minutes to audit and remediate all such failure modes and their root causes."): the breach actions (evaluateMetricTriggers, slaEscalate) run on every 10-minute tick instead of the hourly one, after refreshing sla_breaches_over_120m from v_sla_over_120m (migrations/2026-10-14-sla-120m.sql: every SLA at most 120 minutes); slaEscalate re-alerts a breached issue every 120 minutes, not once a day, and reads alerts.created_at through datetime(). */ /* 0.29.0 (2026-10-14, pillar autonomy): PR-LANE-FAST-1, owner directive "The system shall process PRs more rapidly and push to production.": the stale-PR lane merges a green, clean session pull request after ops_config stale_pr_merge_idle_min of quiet (default 20 minutes, floor 10) instead of 2 hours, and the code loop decides merges on every 10-minute tick instead of twice an hour; every merge gate and the post-deploy canary are unchanged. 0.28.1 (2026-10-14): the journeys accept any 2xx answer as success (WORKERS-STANDARDS-GUARD-1 write-200-only). 0.28.0 (2026-10-14, pillar core): the remediation additions listed after "Also in 0.27.0" below (code tasks, negative control, 5xx, Cloudflare Issues loop, 6 h window, synthetic tag, log noise) ship as their own minor release; VERSION-BUMP-GUARD-1 needs a bump on each push. 0.27.0 (2026-10-13, pillar core): FLEET-JOURNEYS-2, end-to-end journeys baked into fleet control (owner directive: "End-to-end worker functionality testing shall be baked into Cloudflare Quniverse system diagnostics and fleet control"). Every 20 minutes, through service bindings: papers-path (qnfo-gateway list -> page -> feed -> OAI-PMH), lock-roundtrip (qnfo-deploy-guard acquire/list/release/list), binding-census and deploy-coherence (qnfo-ops /fleet; a registry version that disagrees with the worker's own is corrected in the loop and logged to self_heal_actions), loop-heartbeats (dashboard, ai-search, gateway loops), ai-router (qnfo-ai, qnfo-pdf), traffic-health (real-traffic error rate per worker from worker_logs and analytics_dash_workers, naming the top failing route) and, every 6 h, ask-path. Each hop is recorded (journey_runs.path_json); GET /journeys serves the newest runs, the hop graph and the fixes; one self-closing FLEET-JOURNEY-FAILED-1 issue per failing journey, shared with scripts/fleet_journeys.py; metric fleet_journeys_failing. Bindings SVC_QNFO_GATEWAY, SVC_QNFO_AI_SEARCH, SVC_DEPLOY_GUARD, SVC_QNFO_DASH. ops_config fleet_journeys = off stops it. Also in 0.27.0: JOURNEY-CODE-TASK-1 (a failing hop or real-traffic route answering >= 400 gets code-task and code-anchor lines on its handler, found on main, unique or none), NEGATIVE-CONTROL-1 (a deliberate failure each tick: an impossible paper must 404 and an invalid claim must be refused, or the checks fail open), SERVER-5XX-1 (handled 5xx answers from the Workers telemetry API, checked against Cloudflare Observability Issues so a blind or unfiltered query fails), CF-ISSUES-LOOP-1 (Cloudflare Observability Issues: payload refreshed each poll, rows tracked or resolved instead of stuck 'new', recurring error groups fail traffic-health), TRAFFIC-WINDOW-6H-1, SYNTHETIC-TAG-1 (journey requests carry x-qnfo-synthetic: 1) and LOG-NOISE-1 (expected duplicate-column ALTER answers, trial JSON parses and empty GitHub 204 bodies are no longer logged as errors). */ /* 0.26.5 (2026-10-13, pillar autonomy): HOLDING-OPEN-REARM-2 (agent_issues 2526), its own version so the push that carries it is ahead (VERSION-BUMP-GUARD-1 checks each push): the remediation tick runs an open issue's contract as active at its own cadence and re-arms one issue_refile_reopen left holding; a pass that closed the issue still takes the post-close hold. */ /* 0.26.4 (2026-10-13, pillar autonomy; owner directive: issues resolved, deployed and closed within 2 hours): OBS-REASSERT-LEDGER-1 (agent_issues 2520) writes the SETTINGS-ONLY fleet_deploys row for every settings PATCH Cloudflare accepted, verified or not, so qnfo-deploy-guard stops refiling DEPLOY-UNLOGGED-MUTATION for qnfo-containers-pilot; PORTFOLIO-PUT-RETRY-1 (2523) re-reads the sha and PUTs again on HTTP 409/422, at most 3 attempts, in pfCommit and charterCommit; COE-NULL-ID-WRITER-1 (2519) gives the six cloud_ops_events writes an id and an ISO ts and compares the dispose-blocked dedupes and llm_gateway_log windows through datetime(ts) */ /* 0.26.2 REMEDIATION-2X-1 (2026-10-13, pillar autonomy; owner directive "All issue remediation and consumer runs shall be quickened/increased a minimum of 100% (2x). All issues shall be remediated/resolved/drained/deployed faster than they accumulate."): the 20-minute cron runs every 10 minutes; the remediation tick, code-loop PR opening, the stale-PR lane and the deploy-drift runner run every 10 minutes (were 20), the code-loop merge decisions run at minute 30 as well as on the hourly tick, and a probed contract is due again after half its earlier offset (hourly: 18 minutes, was 35). The other 20-minute steps keep their grid. */ /* 0.26.1 CI-FEEDBACK-ORDER-1 (2026-10-13, pillar autonomy): a refused code-loop pull request's CI excerpt lists the failing suites and assertions first; runtime-error lines that passing suites print fill only the lines left (ct_j25aciskebfq1f read personal-api log noise instead of its failing suite). */ /* 0.26.0 DEPLOY-DRIFT-CF-1 (2026-10-13, pillars core and autonomy): the 20-minute tick is the deploy's second runner on Cloudflare (spof_registry GitHub Actions): a canonical-path worker whose main VERSION has been ahead of live for 45 minutes, with no canonical-deploy run active, is deployed through qnfo-ops POST /ops/deploy on the new SVC_QNFO_OPS binding (props.caller), at most 2 a tick; control-plane workers are skipped; ops_config deploy_drift_cf = off stops it. */ /* 0.25.0 METRIC-REFRESHER-2 (2026-10-13, pillar autonomy): the 20-minute tick is a second path for the four metrics only D1 triggers on fleet_tick wrote (audits_stale and the three publish-freshness metrics): same SQL, writes when the trigger path is stale, shadows otherwise; a clean run moves the two spof_registry rows to spof_registry_resolved. */ /* 0.24.1 LARGE-FILE-READ-1 (2026-10-13, pillar autonomy): the merge runner (cmRead) and evReadFile read a file above 1 MB through the git blobs API; the contents API returns no content past 1 MB, so every code-loop task on qnfo-research-exec/worker.js was refused at merge. */ // 0.24.0 RESEARCH-BACKPRESSURE-1 (agent_issues 2193): the 20-minute tick keeps at most research_ready_cap rows (default 3) of research_queue in status queued, chosen by priority (remediation, owner-authored, score, age), and holds the rest in a visible deferred pool released as executor slots free; research_ready stamps when a row became ready so research_queued_180m measures the wait for an executor; ops_config research_backpressure = off releases the pool. // 0.23.0 REMEDIATION-TICK-SLOT-1 (agent_issues 2461, 2199): the remediation tick runs on the light 20-minute cron with a 25 s budget instead of inside the hourly fan-out, where about 25 parallel jobs starve its sequential D1 probes and the event ends 30 s after the handler returns (2026-10-13 04:00 and 05:00 UTC: 10 and 11 probes, against about 150 before, so 203 active contracts went overdue); a probed contract is due again 25 minutes before its cadence so an hourly contract is re-probed inside its 60-minute window. /* 0.22.1 MERGE-RUNNER-READS-HOLDS-1: evMergePr reads the PR's HOLD comments before every merge, so the code-task and evolve runners honour a review hold as the stale-PR lane does (PR 1061 was merged 34 minutes after a HOLD); a held PR answers 423 and stays open. */ /* 0.22.0 CHAOS-DRILL-1 (2026-10-12, agent_issues 2180, pillar autonomy; doctrine section 10): every 6 h the hourly tick re-tests each resolved single point of failure's alternate path from spof_alternate_probes (a D1 evidence probe; the qnfo-pdf relay batch and the qnfo-ai router-down drill are forced first), stamps alternate_tested_at on both registers on a pass, files one CHAOS-DRILL-FAILED-1 issue per failing component and closes it on the next pass; metric spof_alternates_untested_24h, event chaos-drill. pdfBacklogRelay takes a force flag for the drill. 0.21.0 OBSERVABILITY-DRIFT-WATCH-1 (2026-10-12, agent_issues 2394, pillar core): the observability reassert reads each worker's declared [observability] blocks from main and holds the live settings to them (declared keys over live), instead of forcing every worker to logs, traces and issues at rate 1, which overwrote a declared rate on the next tick (qnfo-ai traces 0.1 read live 1) and made the declared config inert; a worker that declares nothing keeps the fleet default. Each run writes metric observability_drift_unrepaired (workers still drifting after the patch) and a cloud_ops_events obs-drift-repair row naming the repaired workers and keys. 0.20.1 ADVISOR-BACKLOG-DEDUPE-1 (2026-10-12, #2159, pillar autonomy): the 20-minute advisor audit no longer files its OPEN-ISSUES-BACKLOG ticket (metric open_agent_issues, trigger 362, issue 1798 owns that signal; the ticket reopened itself through issue_refile_reopen after every supersede) and closes any open one through issue_triage.close_evidence as superseded. 0.20.0 STALE-PR-LANE-READS-HOLDS-1 (2026-10-12, #2389, pillar autonomy): before the lane merges a quiet green pull request it reads the newest issue comments and the head commit's date; a comment newer than the head that asks for changes (HOLD:, do not merge, changes requested, "before this merges") refuses the merge with "a review comment asks for changes" and keeps the PR open, until a later comment says resolved or hold released, a new head commit lands, or the hold is 24 h old (logged as expired); comments the lane wrote (STALE-PR-, CYCLE-TIME-) never count. CONTROL-PLANE-FUNCTIONAL-CANARY-1 (#2176): the code loop's deny list (CM_DENY) no longer carries qnfo-ai and qnfo-gateway, which canonical-deploy canaries with a functional request (scripts/canary_revert.py FUNCTIONAL) and reverts on its own; the lane's control-plane handling (CM_CONTROL_PLANE: canary + mirror pair) still covers them. 0.19.5 PDF-RELAY-CADENCE-1 (2026-10-12, #2410): the relay runs every 20-minute tick while the pdf cron is silent (quiet window 15 min, was 25), takes the 90 s budget and chains up to three batches a tick. 0.19.4 WORKERS-BP-DEBT-1 (#2429, #2395, pillar security): the advisor route compares ADVISOR_TOKEN with secretEq, and the four Math.random ids and the multipart boundary take crypto.getRandomValues (randHex); the standing fail-class findings for this worker read 0. 0.19.3 (0.19.2 merged with main 0.18.2; every pushed byte change takes a bump) UNIFIED-COST-BYOK-DEFAULT-1 (#2423, pillar cost): the BYOK default names deepseek, anthropic and openai, so unified_cost_usd_30d stops counting our own-key Anthropic and OpenAI gateway requests as gateway-billed. 0.19.1 (0.19.0 plus the relay error-recording fix caught by pdf-relay.test.mjs) PDF-BACKLOG-RELAY-1 (#2410, 2026-10-12, pillar reach): the twenty-minute tick relays qnfo-pdf POST /backlog/tick through the new SVC_QNFO_PDF service binding whenever no pdf-backlog event has landed for 25 minutes, because the ten-minute cron written for qnfo-pdf at 12:04Z never fired (zero scheduled invocations over four ticks while every other ten-minute worker fired); ledger cloud_ops_events kind pdf-backlog-relay. Also MVP-FOLD-LATEST-1 (#2259, 2026-10-12, pillar core): the charter MVP fold map takes the latest fold row per worker instead of requiring the latest row of any kind to be a fold; the D1 trigger worker_removals_from_live_audit appends OBSERVED-REMOVED when a folded script is deleted, which hid six folds (qnfo-paper-reviser -> qnfo-research-exec among them) and refiled CHARTER-MVP-DOWN-1 against a serving host; a later RESURRECTED/RESTORED/UNFOLDED/REDEPLOYED row still ends the fold. Merged on main 0.18.2 (PR 1000 and its CodeQL follow-up) on 2026-10-12 and numbered above it. Prior: 0.18.1 REGEX-ESCAPE-1 + MD-CELL-ESCAPE-1 (CodeQL js/incomplete-sanitization on four lines of this file): a name put into a RegExp is escaped whole, and a Markdown table cell (charter, portfolio) escapes a backslash before the pipe. 0.18.0 the merge side of the code loop (owner directive 2026-10-12; issue 2074): GOAL-REVIEW-2 (a goal-review refusal needs two reviewers of different model families; each defect quotes the changed line it is about and is screened against the diff and the file at the head; VERSION, comment and style remarks never refuse; the reviewer reads the whole goal, the diff with long lines shown around their change, and the names the file defines), REFUSAL-REASON-1 + REPAIR-AT-OPEN-1 (a refusal reaches the planner's repair round as ctx.refusal and ctx.lastError, at the open step too), PATCH-REBUILD-1 + MIRROR-FOLLOWS-SOURCE-1 (a change that no longer fits its base is rebuilt from its parked edits or re-proposed, never a dead end; a publish_failed conflict goes back to the orchestrator), MERGE-MULTI-FILE-1 (ctx.paths companions, new files, ctx.x[].edits; ops_config code_merge_multi_file), MERGEABILITY-REQUERY-1 + LANE-TICK-20-1 (the stale-PR lane pre-warms and re-reads a null mergeability before any update-branch, and runs every 20 minutes), PUBLISH-DISPATCH-1 (code-task-publish.yml is dispatched when a task has been ready_to_publish for 10 minutes; ops_config code_publish_dispatch_enabled). 0.17.0 MERGEABILITY-NUDGE-1 + MERGE-REFUSAL-LOG-1 (#2230): a green quiet session PR whose GitHub mergeability stays null (or whose branch is only behind main) gets PUT /pulls/{n}/update-branch pinned to its head and is kept, at most 3 times in 24h (ops_config stale_pr_nudge_enabled), and every non-merge is a branch_hygiene_log row merge-nudge or merge-refused (one per PR, head and reason). STALE-PR-CONFLICT-REPAIR-1 (#2304, carried from PR 910): a quiet PR that conflicts with main gets one deduped high-priority issue with the re-apply procedure (ops_config stale_pr_conflict_repair_enabled). SECRET-COMPARE-1: 32 token comparisons are constant-time; SECURE-ID-1: code task ids come from crypto.getRandomValues. Prior: 0.16.1 PERF-PIN-1 (#2177): ops_config perf_pin:<lever> takes one knob out of the performance loop's search space, so the loop can run again while the owner's q08_max_per_day stays untouched. 0.16.0 CODE-REPAIR-INTASK-1 (owner directive 2026-10-11, deploy success): a goal-review or required-check refusal of an open code-loop PR sends the task back to propose with the defects or failing suite as feedback, on a fresh branch, up to 2 rounds, instead of failing it.  0.13.1: the repair filing also writes cloud_ops_events kind stale-pr-check-repair (the issue-2122 contract proof). 0.13.0 STALE-PR-CHECK-REPAIR-1 (agent_issues 2122): a quiet session PR that is green on every required check but fails only a non-required check (CodeQL) is never merged; the branch sweeper now files one agent_issue per such PR with the failing runs' annotations and a code-task line naming the annotated file, so the finding is fixed instead of the PR being closed unmerged at 24h. */ /* 0.12.2 COST-RUN-RATE-2 (owner request 2026-10-09): fleet_budget ai_spend caps meter the 7-day run rate x 30 from v_cost_run_rate (the daily all-billing cost ledger) instead of a 30-day window; the 30-day figures remain the fallback. */ /* 0.12.1 DETECTOR-CADENCE-1: standing detectors (fm-*, belief-*) are exempt from REMEDIATION-HOLD-1, so failure-mode and belief audits run hourly instead of parking 24 h and closing after 7 days. */ /* 0.12.0 PORTFOLIO-CODE-PUBLISH-1 (#2062, card code-repos-create): the daily portfolio sync creates each staged research-code library's public repository with the fleet token and copies research-code/<name>/ into it (at most 3 per sync, existing files never replaced), then marks the row public. */ /* 0.11.7 CHARTER_VERSION 1.0.14 (DOCTRINE-1, charter section 8 rule 13); no behaviour change. */ /* 0.11.6 CHARTER_VERSION 1.0.13 (ANTIFRAGILE-1, charter section 8 rule 12); no behaviour change. */ /* 0.11.5 QUEUE-SLA-1 (2026-10-08, pillar autonomy, owner directive "No issue shall remain unprocessed/unremediated for greater than 3 hours"): the remediation tick evaluates up to 150 due contracts per run (was 15): 94 of 136 open issues had no probe verdict in 3 h because 15 per hourly tick could not cover them; migrations/2026-10-08-queue-sla.sql makes every open-issue contract due hourly. */ /* 0.11.4 AUTONOMY-FIRST-1 (2026-10-08, pillar autonomy): CHARTER_VERSION 1.0.12, charter section 8 rule 11 (autonomy first: the only owner interrupt is an action both irreversible and identity-bound; enforced on the owner queue by migrations/2026-10-08-autonomy-first.sql); no behaviour change in this worker. */ /* 0.11.3 PROMPT-CACHE-COUNT-4 (issue 2115, 2026-10-08, pillar cost): aiRunAttr also writes the ai_cache_counters row (qnfo-ops form) for text models, so fleet-control and qnfo-fleet-control calls count toward the cached-input share. */  /* 0.11.2 REBASE-INTEGRITY-1 (2026-10-07, pillar autonomy): cmIntegrity judges a branch code-task-publish rebuilt from ctx.edits on current main (REBASE-BEFORE-PUBLISH-1, ctx.rebased) by re-applying those edits at the merge base and bumping the VERSION as the publisher does, instead of the parked ctx.patch that was cut against the old base; its revert inverts the edits on today's main. The first rebuilt branch to pass REBASE-BRANCH-ACCEPT-1 (codeagent-3oa9p0pglnnj-r2, 17:20Z) was refused at this gate ("the verified patch does not apply to idea-hub/deployed-current.worker.js at the merge base 0ac2898"), so the no-model rebase path still produced no pull request. */ /* 0.11.1 OWNER-LOCAL-INGEST-1b (2026-10-07, pillar cost, agent_issues 2080): the gateway log ingest asks the API for paid non-Workers-AI rows after its cursor (filters cost gt 0, provider neq workers-ai, created_at gt cursor), oldest first, 20 pages a tick, so the cursor only ever advances over rows it ingested and a 7-day backfill completes over a few ticks; 0.11.0 read the newest 500 of all rows newest first (418,943 in the gateway, 69 of each 100 Workers AI), reached 7 hours back on its first tick, moved the cursor to the newest row and attributed none of the 4,991 untagged DeepSeek requests of the week (measured 2026-10-07T16:15Z, about $15). Cursor key owner_local_cursor_v2:<gateway>; the v1 key is removed; the event meta reports more and remaining. Also REBASE-BRANCH-ACCEPT-1 (pillar autonomy): cmOpenDecide and cmDecide accept a task's -r<n> rebuilt branch (cmTaskBranch), so a REBASE-REQUEUE-1 rebuild gets its pull request (codeagent-3oa9p0pglnnj-r2 was refused as "not a code-loop branch" at 15:20Z, the path's first live instance); and ISSUE-NOTE-NEWLINE-1: the merge runner's note on a source issue (and the evolve merge note) starts on its own line instead of " | " on the issue's last line, which was the code-anchor: line of 10 open ACT-BRIDGE-1 issues, so their retries ran anchor-less (migrations/2026-10-07-issue-note-newline.sql repairs the open rows). */ /* 0.11.0 OWNER-LOCAL-INGEST-1 (2026-10-07, pillar cost, agent_issues 2080): the hourly tick reads each AI Gateway's request log since a per-gateway cursor and attributes the paid cost: untagged requests (the owner's desktop clients) to ai_spend_owner_local, requests tagged by a fleet worker that keeps no ledger of its own to ai_spend_ledger under that worker; cost_attribution_gap_pct counts both (it read 98 with $21.77 of 7-day DeepSeek cost unattributed), the dashboard gets owner_local_cost_usd_30d. */ /* 0.10.0 SCOPE-SCRIPTS-1 (2026-10-07, pillar autonomy, issue 2101): the merge runner's scope gains kind "script": scripts/*.py and scripts/*.mjs that are not CI gates or guards, suites, deploy primitives or the loop's own runners (CM_SCRIPT_DENY), so a fleet script defect can be a code task instead of session work (issue 2025 sat with a session-task line for scripts/cf_ops_actions.py only because of the scope). A script merges on gate, mirror-guard and comparator (deploy-gate runs the script selftests) and is verified at merge; nothing deploys it. */ /* 0.9.1 GOAL-REVIEW-HARM-1 (2026-10-07, pillar autonomy): the goal reviewer also answers harm (true when any changed line is wrong: breaks or removes kept behaviour, adds code that can never run, miscounts, contradicts a stated rule, would throw), and harm refuses whatever the verdict. The first live review (ct_hdaim0vx7h7vvl, 08:40Z, gpt-oss-120b) answered partial while naming two errors, an unreachable else that still incremented diversity_held and owner rows not forced to ACCEPT, so the runner opened PR 765, which a session closed as superseded by PR 762. A cached review without harm decides as before. 0.9.0 0.9.0 GOAL-REVIEW-1 (2026-10-07, pillar autonomy, docs/ENSEMBLE-POLICY.md): before the merge runner opens or merges a code-loop pull request, one Workers AI model from a family other than the proposer's (CM_REVIEW_MODELS gpt-oss-120b, deepseek-v4-flash, llama-3.3-70b; ops_config code_goal_review_models) reads the goal and the head diff and answers implements, partial or no; "no" refuses the task with the defects it names, which reach the intake retry through CI-FEEDBACK-1. One call per head, cached in cloud_ops_events goal-review-<task>-<head>, metered as purpose goal-review; no AI binding or ops_config code_goal_review_enabled off skips it; three unreadable replies let the checks decide (recorded). Of the three tasks self-repair rescued on 2026-10-06/07, #2052's patch only passed [] to the removed deposit stage and #1815's wrote living-paper columns no migration creates and labelled a paper "proved" when its body said "proof"; no check could see either. Also 0.8.2 MERGE-VERIFY-ATTEMPTS-1 (2026-10-07, pillar autonomy): the merge runner's verify gate accepts a task that verified after SELF-REPAIR-1 retries (attempts below CM_TASK_MAX_ATTEMPTS 9, the orchestrator's MAX_ATTEMPTS * RETRY_ROUNDS, parity-tested) instead of attempts below 3; step done with no last_error stays the record of a passed verify, and the required checks still gate every merge. The old bound refused all three tasks self-repair rescued (ct_yop1itun7a9ulz #1815, ct_vdgdp57qdszmkb #2052, ct_i0b4q32jxbvia7 #2055), each a failure in code_task_success_rate_30d with a verified patch. 0.8.1 0.8.1 MVP-FOLD-NOTDEPLOYED-1 (2026-10-07, pillar core, agent_issues 2090-2094): a folded MVP component is judged by its fold host unless its own audit row still serves (SYNC, CRON_ONLY or http 200); 0.4.129 deferred to the host only while the old script was absent from the audit or RETIRED_PRESENT, so after cf-ops delete-worker its row read NOT_DEPLOYED (404) and calendar-api, fleet-exec, qnfo-autonomy-scorer, qnfo-paper-indexer and qnfo-paper-reviser filed CHARTER-MVP-DOWN-1 while every host was SYNC. 0.8.0 0.8.0 CI-FEEDBACK-1 (2026-10-07, pillar autonomy): when a required check fails on a code-loop pull request, the merge runner reads that job's log and records the failing suites and assertion lines (cmFailureLines, at most 10 lines) in the refusal, so the task's merge_note and its issue say what broke and the next intake retry carries it; before this the note said only "gate=failure" and every retry was blind (PR 750 broke qnfo-ipatent/mechanism.test.mjs, PR 752 changed a value quality.test.mjs:190 pins). merge_note and last_error keep 1200 characters (was 500). 0.7.1 (2026-10-06, pillar autonomy): CHARTER_VERSION 1.0.11 in parity with the charter, which adds decision rule 10 "decide, then record" (RULE-8-RETIRED-1, owner directive 2026-10-06: core prompt rule 8 is deleted); one comment no longer cites rule 8. 0.7.0 CONTROL-PLANE-SELF-MERGE-1 (2026-10-06, transformation lever T1.21, pillar autonomy; owner directive 2026-10-06: more flexibility and autonomy, decide for itself): the stale-PR lane merges a green, quiet session pull request that changes a control-plane worker (CM_DENY) when ops_config control_plane_self_merge is on, the worker has a /health canary (CP_CANARY_WORKERS) and the pull request carries worker.js with its mirror; canonical-deploy.yml canaries /health for the new VERSION and reverts the push on its own (scripts/canary_revert.py, CONTROL-PLANE-CANARY-1), which replaces CONTROL-PLANE-MANUAL-1 (decision (a), human_actions 21, migrations/2026-10-06-control-plane-self-merge.sql). Workflows under .github/ still never auto-merge; the code loop still neither plans nor merges control-plane workers. 0.6.2 CRAWL-VERIFIED-GOOGLEBOT-1 (2026-10-06, pillar reach): the crawl-health view counts only requests from Google's published Googlebot ranges (googlebot.json, fallback 66.249.64.0/19); spoofed Googlebot scans are reported, not counted; a robots.txt 404 is not a failure; sitemap failures only for CRAWL_SITEMAPS. 0.6.1 (2026-10-06, pillar cost): CHARTER_VERSION 1.0.10 in parity with the charter, which records BUDGET-SOFT-ROUTE-1 (owner directive: AI spend caps steer model choice and never stop work). 0.6.0 PROBE-TRANSPORTS-1 (2026-10-06, pillar autonomy; owner directive OWNER-NO-LOOSE-ENDS-1): remediation contracts can check public sources outside the fleet: transport external-https (GET or HEAD on an allowlist of GitHub, PyPI, DOI, OpenAlex, Crossref and DataCite, https only, no credentials, redirects observed not followed, status, header, body-contains or json check; expected from the probe, observed from the response; contracts on fleet hosts are left to the off-Cloudflare executor of agent_issues 2060, issue 1190) and d1-query@portfolio-state (the PORTFOLIO binding) join d1-query; verification rows record the transport. 0.5.0 DANGLING-BINDINGS-1 (2026-10-06, transformation lever T9.4, pillar core): the 03:00Z tick runs danglingBindingsCensus, every live script's settings (CF API workers/scripts/<name>/settings) against the account's D1, KV, R2, queue, Vectorize and script lists; dangling_bindings is the count (migrations/2026-10-06-dangling-bindings.sql: guard metric, trigger gt 0, contract) and cloud_ops_events dangling-bindings-<day> names script, binding, kind and target; unverifiable binding types and unreadable lists count as unchecked, never as dangling; the WATCHMAKER_OPS entry dangling-bindings-census is code task DANGLING-BINDINGS-WATCHMAKER-1 (agent_issues 2051). Also PORTFOLIO-ARCHIVE-1 (REPO-ARCHIVE-1, agent_issues 2045): pfHygieneApply executes explicit portfolio_actions archive-request rows (PATCH archived=true, reversible, at most PF_ARCHIVE_MAX per sync, never a delete; docs/PORTFOLIO.md rule 3), because a session's GitHub proxy refuses repository settings writes. 0.4.140 CRAWL-HEALTH-Q08-1: the Googlebot check also reads the q08.org zone and its sitemap; 0.4.139 ONE-WORKER-COUNT-1 + COST-ATTRIBUTION-GAP-1 + REBASE-REQUEUE-1 (2026-10-06, transformation levers T5.10, T4.7 and T1.3 half 2; pillars core, cost, autonomy): budgetAudit writes metric_registry.worker_count from the live scripts census it already writes to fleet_budget.workers and worker_count_disagreement (guard) from its comparison with service_registry state live (the names in cloud_ops_events worker-count-<day>; qnfo-lifecycle stops writing worker_count); refreshOwnedMetrics writes cost_attribution_gap_pct, the share of the paid AI Gateway list cost of the last 7 days that has no ai_spend_ledger row (per provider and the models with the largest cost in cloud_ops_events cost-attribution-<day>; 98.7% on 2026-10-06, most of it a Node client with no cf-aig-metadata); cmRequeueStale hands a stale task that parked its SEARCH/REPLACE edits back to code-task-publish (status ready_to_publish, branch <branch>-r2) for a rebuild on current main without a model call (REBASE-BEFORE-PUBLISH-1), once, before re-proposing; numbered above main's 0.4.138 (main took 0.4.135 to 0.4.138 while this change was open: PRs 699, 707, 709). 0.4.138 CRAWL-HEALTH-1: Googlebot sitemap and error view from the zone request log, self-filing and self-closing; 0.4.137 SEARCH-REFERRALS-1: search_referrals_30d and google_referrals_30d from Cloudflare RUM referrers each reach tick; 0.4.136 metric column fix; 0.4.135 GOOGLE-IDENTITY-DETECT-1: the reach tick resolves the owner Google card from public DNS; 0.4.134 W0-LEADING-EXIT-1 (2026-10-06, pillar autonomy, docs/TRANSFORMATION-PROGRAM.md 1.2 T1 lever 16): wave W0 exits on code_task_success_rate_engine, the success rate (merged over finished, the formula of code_task_success_rate_30d) of code tasks created after lever (1, 15) MERGE-SCOPE-INTAKE-1 landed, measured only once at least TP_ENGINE_MIN_FINISHED (8) have finished; the 42 closures of 2026-10-02..10-05 stay in the 30-day window until November whatever the engine does now, so W0 measured the past. code_task_success_rate_30d keeps its scoreboard row and its trigger. 0.4.133 SCORER-HOST-DENY-1 (2026-10-06, pillar autonomy, docs/TRANSFORMATION-PROGRAM.md 1.2 section 1.12): EVOLVE_DENY (so CM_DENY) and TP_CONTROL_PLANE name qnfo-observability. qnfo-autonomy-scorer was denied so that no loop merges a change to the formula that grades the fleet; SCORER-FOLD-1 (PR 668) moved that code into qnfo-observability, which the merge runner and the planner then accepted. A FOLDED worker's host now inherits its place, and fold-guard.test.mjs fails CI when a marker names a denied guest whose host is not denied, or when this list, the transformation loop's and the orchestrator's PLAN_DENY_WORKERS differ. 0.4.132 TRANSFORMATION-LOOP-1 (2026-10-06, owner directive 2026-10-06, pillar autonomy; 0.4.132 adds TP-1a TRUSTED-ORIGIN-PARITY-1 (agent_issues 2005: the CM_TRUSTED_SOURCES default carries every pair the orchestrator planner trusts plus the TP- origins, parity-tested in code-merge.test.mjs), the W1 exit counting needs-machine-probe contracts on open issues only (closed ones on their own scoreboard row, document 1.1 section 1.10), and TP-WAVE-EXIT-STALLED-1, filed when an unmet exit metric of the active wave reads the same value in metric_history 14 days apart): the engine docs/TRANSFORMATION-PROGRAM.md section 5 describes, on the hourly tick: transformation_levers (one row per lever, seeded by migrations/2026-10-06-transformation-loop.sql), wave state from the section 4 exit metrics, dispatch of the next eligible code lever as a code-task issue (session-task for refactor, retire, migration, platform and control-plane levers; TP_SESSION_MAX open at once), landing from merged code tasks and closed issues, 14-day stall detection (TP-LEVER-STALLED-1), session fallback (CODE-TASK-NEEDS-SESSION-1), the section 6 scoreboard in transformation_runs, metric transformation_levers_landed_14d, GET /transformation and POST /transformation/tick; no new cron, worker, binding or model call. 0.4.128 REMEDIATION-PENDING-PREFIX-1 (pillar autonomy): a probe observation that starts with 'pending' (the 'pending: <reason>' form six live contracts use) is a deferral like a bare 'pending': it neither breaks a hold, reopens a closed issue, counts toward max_attempts nor ends a pass streak; 0.4.130 PR-OPEN-ON-20MIN-TICK-1 (agent_issues 2017, TP-1b2, pillar autonomy): the 20-minute cron also runs codeMergeTick(env, { openOnly: true }), which only opens pull requests for branch_pushed code tasks (no advance, no merge decision, no reconciliation, no day heartbeat) and stands aside at minute 0 where the hourly tick runs; measured 2026-10-06, a pushed codeagent branch waited 40-50 min for its PR on every task (pr_opened_at always hh:00) and 5 h overnight because only the hourly tick opened them, while code-task-publish had pushed the branch within a minute. CHARTER-1.0.9: CHARTER_VERSION 1.0.9 for the charter's TRANSFORMATION-PROGRAM-1 input pointer (PR 664), charter-guard C5 parity, no behaviour change. 0.4.129 MVP-FOLD-AWARE-1 (pillar core, #1756): an MVP component recorded as folded into a host (worker_removals action folded, target host) serves when its host serves, so folding a core worker under the owner standing grant does not file CHARTER-MVP-D